  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Light rain showers continue across\nportions of Humboldt county this afternoon and are expected into\nthis evening. Rainfall amounts as seen from some remote \nobservation platforms for the morning are coming in with a tenth\nor so, though twenty-four hour totals of a third of an inch was \nrecorded at Texas Springs and Double H. Further east and south,\nskies are mostly sunny. There is an upper level low pressure \nsystem across northwest Oregon at this time and is responsible for\nbringing the light precipitation to Humboldt county. Southwest \nflow across central and northeast Nevada are keeping skies mostly\nsunny. For tonight, expect any rain showers to diminish during \nthe overnight with skies gradually clearing. Overnight lows will \nbe in the 40s.\n\nSouthwest flow will remain over northern and central Nevada\nSaturday. Skies are expected to be mostly sunny through the day\nwith highs in the 70s and 80s. Winds will again be breezy to\nlocally windy across central Nevada with gusts to 35 mph in the\nafternoon. Other locales will see occasional breezy conditions.\nHigh temperatures will be in the 70s and 80s once again. Overnight\nlows will be in the 40s.\n\nA piece of energy will move around the base of the trough across\nnorthern California and northwest Nevada for Sunday. Some \nmoisture from a tropical cyclone in the eastern Pacific will be \npicked up by the upper trough, bringing rain showers to the north \nand central locales. Amounts are expected to be on the light side \nwith amounts of five-hundredths to a tenth. Highs will remain in \nthe 70s and 80s with lows in the 40s and 50s. \n\nFrom Monday through Friday, generally dry conditions are expected\nto persist though there are possible opportunities for light rain\nshowers or a thunderstorm each afternoon from roughly Wednesday\nthrough the end of the period. Confidence is quite low at this\ntime in this scenario. Afternoon high temperatures will be in the\n70s and 80s with lows in the 40s and 50s. Afternoon breezes to 20\nto 25 mph will be possible each afternoon.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in cool\ntemperatures and strong winds through the weekend. Weekend storm\nconfidence continues to be moderate, with low confidence in storm\npotential next week. No changes were made from the NBM forecast.",
